# Implementation Plan - Flex Message Display

The current [MessageList](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#34-104) component does not have a rendering case for `FLEX` messages, so they are not displayed in the chat interface.

## User Review Required

> [!NOTE]
> Rendering full Flex Message JSON exactly as it appears in LINE is complex (requires a dedicated Flex renderer library or iframe).
> For this version, I will implement a **simplified display**:
> - Show the `altText` of the Flex message (which is what shows up in push notifications).
> - If `altText` is missing, show "[Flex Message]".
> - This ensures admins at least know a message was sent and what it was generally about.

## Proposed Changes

### Chat Components

#### [MODIFY] [message-list.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx)
- Update [MessageBubble](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#105-166) component to handle `contentType === "FLEX"` (or "flex", generally case-insensitive or checked against the stored value).
- Extract `altText` from the content payload if available.
- Render a styled bubble for Flex messages.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1.  Send a text broadcast (already working).
2.  Send a **Flex Broadcast** (using Postman or if the UI supports it, otherwise I can manually insert a test record or use the worker to send one).
3.  Check the chat interface.
4.  Verify that a bubble appears with the text "[Flex Message]" or the specific alt text.
